7.2.m:
Delightful is this threefold world for that person;
all his enemies perish together with their clans;
his friends and all his kinsmen prosper,
upon whom you look with compassions here, O lord of immortals.

7.5.m:
Candrakalā said:
“On her left hip there is a mole resembling a sesame seed;
by the sight of that alone you will recognize Sulocanā.

Vyāsa said:
Then that prince returned home along with his army;
and that virtuous Candrakalā, well-pleased, went to her own home.

Mādhava said:
“You are all noble-minded, endowed with all auspicious marks;
which horse among you is able to carry me to the other shore of the ocean?”

The horse said:
“I will take you to the shore of the ocean, there is no doubt;
but listen to my sorrows, O prince.

Mādhava said:
“Forgive all the fault committed by my father, O horse;
from this day forward you are the foremost within my stable.
